ill show you the Calculate Performance Conditions menu as shown in Figure 1.4.\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\sl240\slmult1\sb12\f0\fs20\b0\i0\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li360\ri1037\sl249\slmult1\f0\fs20\b0\expnd0\expndtw0\charscalex100 For now, leave all the Calculation Conditions as they\expnd-1\expndtw-4  \expnd0\expndtw0 are and click on the Calculate Performance button.\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 This will start the program calculating performance for the specifications of the 96 Mustang GT stored in the Vehicle Library with the Calculation Conditions currently displayed.\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 A progress bar graph shows how the calculations are progressing.\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 The calculations may require several seconds on slower computers.\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\sl240\slmult1\sb13\f0\fs20\b0\i0\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li359\ri941\sl249\slmult1\f0\fs20\b0\expnd0\expndtw0\charscalex100 The final results will appear in a table as in Figure 1.5.\expnd15\expndtw74  \expnd0\expndtw0 The columns are for various types of readings (Gear #, MPH, etc) which occurred at critical points in the run, like the start, the end of each gear, beginning of each gear, 60 foot time, 60 MPH, \expnd-1\expndtw-4 etc.\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\sl240\slmult1\f0\fs20\b0\i0\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\sl240\slmult1\sb23\f0\fs20\b0\i0\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li359\ri1277\sl249\slmult1\f0\fs20\b0\expnd0\expndtw0\charscalex100 The results contain much information, some which may\expnd-1\expndtw-6  \expnd0\expndtw0 not be familiar to\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 you.\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 However, the first three columns do\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 look familiar:\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 Gear, Time and MPH.\par\sect\sectd\sbkpage\headery731\footery748\margtsxn1120\margbsxn94