e the Engine Analyzer.\par\pard\plain\s11\ls12\ilvl0\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li1079\fi-360\ri6152\sl249\slmult1\sb4\tx1079\f0\fs20\b0\expnd0\expndtw0\charscalex100 The Drag Racing Analyzer Pro\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 will be automatically activated and run.\par\pard\plain\s11\ls12\ilvl0\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li1079\fi-360\ri5556\sl249\slmult1\sb1\tx1079\f0\fs20\b0\expnd0\expndtw0\charscalex100 When the Drag Racing Analyzer Pro starts up the first time, you are given notice that a power curve is available and can be loaded from the Engine specs menu.\expnd16\expndtw80  \expnd0\expndtw0 You will also\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 notice some new commands on the Main Menu called \'93Engine Analyzer\'94.\expnd16\expndtw80\charscalex150  \expnd0\expndtw0\charscalex100 Clicking on\expnd6\expndtw29  \expnd0\expndtw0 these will\expnd5\expndtw25  \expnd0\expndtw0 return\expnd6\expndtw29  \expnd0\expndtw0 to control to the Engine Analyzer program which originally called the Drag Racing Analyzer Pro, but will leave the\expnd16\expndtw80  \expnd0\expndtw0 Drag Racing Analyzer Pro also running, ready for a new power curve.\par\pard\plain\s11\ls12\ilvl0\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li1079\fi-360\ri938\sl249\slmult1\sb8\tx1079\f0\fs20\b0\expnd0\expndtw0\charscalex100 Important:\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 Once\expnd0\expndtw-2  \expnd0\expndtw0 you load the\expnd0\expndtw-2  \expnd0\expndtw0 power curve, the\expnd0\expndtw-2  \expnd0\expndtw0 old power curve\expnd0\expndtw-2  \expnd0\expndtw0 is gone, unless you saved the\expnd0\expndtw-2  \expnd0\expndtw0 vehicle\expnd0\expndtw-2  \expnd0\expndtw0 specs including power curve with the Save command or saved it as an Example by\expnd0\expndtw-2  \expnd0\expndtw0 clicking on File, then Save As at the top of the Engine specs menu.\par\pard\plain\s11\ls12\ilvl0\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li1079\fi-360\ri803\qj\sl249\slmult1\sb2\tx1079\f0\fs20\b0\expnd0\expndtw0\charscalex100 When you are ready\expnd