\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li806\ri608\sl249\slmult1\sb491\f0\fs20\b0\expnd0\expndtw0\charscalex100 The\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 following section explains the\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 user input for engine\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 specs listed with Clc\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 buttons.\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 These\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 specs are\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 ones where\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 you can simply enter a value, or click on the Clc button and the program will present a menu of inputs which will calculate that particular parameter.\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 These menus are like computer \'93scratch pads\'94 for calculating specs like Final Drive Ratio, Tire Diameter, etc. from other inputs.\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\sl240\slmult1\sb14\f0\fs20\b0\i0\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li806\sl240\slmult1\f0\fs20\b0\expnd0\expndtw-2\charscalex100 Notes:\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\sl240\slmult1\sb20\f0\fs20\b0\i0\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li806\ri5200\sl249\slmult1\f0\fs20\b0\expnd0\expndtw0\charscalex100 The starting values in each calculation menu are usually\expnd-1\expndtw-5  \expnd0\expndtw0 blanked out when the menu is opened.\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 If there is other information in the program to estimate what one of your input values will be, it may\expnd-1\expndtw-5  \expnd0\expndtw0 be loaded.\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 As shown in Figure 2.31, Vehicle Weight, Engine Cubic Inches and RPM at HP Peak are already\expnd0\expndtw-2  \expnd0\expndtw0 available from other menus in the program, and these values are loaded into the Calculation Menu.\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 You are free to change them to any other value.\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\sl240\slmult1\sb15\f0\fs20\b0\i0\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li806\ri5197\sl249\slmult1\sb1\f0\fs20\b0\expnd0\expndtw0\charscalex100 Once enough specs have been entered, the calculated value(s) at the top of\expnd-1\expndtw-3  \expnd0\expndtw0 the\expnd0\expndtw-2  \expnd0\expndtw0 menu will be\expnd0\expndtw-2  \expnd0\expndtw0 displayed.\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 This calculated value(s) will now be updated each time you change a spec.\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 If you want to use this calculated value, click on Use Calc Value. If the calculated value is within expected limits, it will be loaded into the original menu.\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 If you click on Cancel, you will be returned to the original menu with the original value unchanged.\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 If you click on Help, you will be\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 given a general explanation of calculation menus, and a page # in\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 this section for more info about the particular menu you are using.\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\sl240\slmult1\sb17\f0\fs20\b0\i0\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li806\ri5200\sl249\slmult1\f0\fs20\b0\expnd0\expndtw0\charscalex100 The input values or calculated values in any calculation menu have NO affect on calculated performance\expnd0\expndtw-2  \expnd0\expndtw0 unless you load the\expnd0\expndtw-2  \expnd0\expndtw0 Calculated value into the original menu.\expnd8\expndtw40  \f8\b1\i1\expnd0\expndtw0 If you already know a spec in the\i1  form required by the program, then you have no need to use the calculation menu.\expnd8\expndtw40  \f0\b0\i0\expnd0\expndtw0 For example, if\expnd0\expndtw-2  \expnd0\expndtw0 you know\expnd-1\expndtw-4  \expnd0\expndtw0 the\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 engine\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 makes 420 ft lbs at 4500 and 450 HP at 6000 RPM, then, you have no need to use a calculation menu to calculate Peak Tq and Peak HP.\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\sl240\slmult1\sb7\f0\fs20\b0\i0\par\pard\plain\s8\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li806\sl240\slmult1\f1\fs28\b0\expnd0\expndtw-2\charscalex100 Example\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li806\ri437\sl249\slmult1\sb248\f0\fs20\b0\expnd0\expndtw0\charscalex100 Assume\expnd0\expndtw-2  \expnd0\expndtw0 you want to\expnd-1\expndtw-3  \expnd0\expndtw0 calculate\expnd0\expndtw-2  \expnd0\expndtw0 Peak Torque\expnd0\expndtw-2  \expnd0\expndtw0 and Peak Horsepower for your car, but you know\expnd-1\expndtw-5  \expnd0\expndtw0 very\expnd-2\expndtw-8  \expnd0\expndtw0 little\expnd0\expndtw-2  \expnd0\expndtw0 about the\expnd0\expndtw-2  \expnd0\expndtw0 engine.\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 You could click on one of the Clc buttons by\expnd0\expndtw-2  \expnd0\expndtw0 Peak Torque or Peak Horsepower in the Engine Specs menu.\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 You will be presented with the menu shown in Figure 2.31.\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\sl240\slmult1\sb13\f0\fs20\b0\i0\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li806\ri515\sl249\slmult1\f0\fs20\b0\expnd0\expndtw0\charscalex100 Vehicle Weight, Engine Cubic Inches and RPM at HP Peak are already\expnd-1\expndtw-4  \expnd0\expndtw0 available from other menus in the program, and these values are already loaded into the Calculation Menu.\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 Vehicle Weight and Cubic Inches are accurate for your engine and vehicle so you leave them \'93as is\'94.\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 However, RPM at HP Peak you are not sure of and you may\expnd-1\expndtw-3  \expnd0\expndtw0 change this.\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\sl240\slmult1\sb12\f0\fs20\b0\i0\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li806\ri437\sl249\slmult1\f0\fs20\b0\expnd0\expndtw0\charscalex100 Note\expnd0\expndtw-2  \expnd0\expndtw0 that all inputs are\expnd0\expndtw-2  \expnd0\expndtw0 disabled except Type\expnd0\expndtw-2  \expnd0\expndtw0 of\expnd-1\expndtw-3  \expnd0\expndtw0 C