\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li806\ri437\sl249\slmult1\sb251\f0\fs20\b0\expnd0\expndtw0\charscalex100 The Chain Calculation lets you make several calculations in succession (like links of a chain), each time varying 1 or 2 specs through a range of settings.\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 To get the Chain Calculation screen, enable the Chain Calcs button in the Calculate Performance Conditions screen as shown in Figure 2.67.\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 Then\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li806\ri6415\sl249\slmult1\sb3\f0\fs20\b0\expnd0\expndtw0\charscalex100 the\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 Chain Calcs button to\expnd0\expndtw-2  \expnd0\expndtw0 bring up the\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 screen shown in Figure 2.68.\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\sl240\slmult1\sb11\f0\fs20\b0\i0\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li806\ri6483\sl249\slmult1\sb1\f0\fs20\b0\expnd0\expndtw0\charscalex100 At the Chain Calculations screen, choose the 1 or 2 Categories and specs for those categories doing the Chain Calculation.\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 The Current value in the\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 program is displayed.\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 You can then enter a Start At value and Ending value, and a step size value.\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 For example, in Figure 2.68, the Body & Axle spec of Final Drive Ratio\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 will go\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 through a range of\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 settings of 3.2, 3.4, 3.6, 3.8, 4.0, 4.2, 4.4, 4.6, 4.8, 5.0 and\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li806\ri6740\sl249\slmult1\sb6\f0\fs20\b0\expnd0\expndtw0\charscalex100 5.2.\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 The program calculates the # Steps The program calculates the # Steps, and the total # combinations (displayed at the\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 top in the\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 square brackets [ ] ) so you get an idea of how many calculations will be made.\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\sl240\slmult1\f0\fs20\b0\i0\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\sl240\slmult1\sb24\f0\fs20\b0\i0\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li806\ri6415\sl249\slmult1\f0\fs20\b0\expnd0\expndtw0\charscalex100 Click on the OK button to start the calculations. When finished the\expnd0\expndtw-2  \expnd0\expndtw0 results will be\expnd0\expndtw-2  \expnd0\expndtw0 displayed in a table as shown in Figure 2.69.\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 From this table you can print the results or graph the results, as shown in\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li806\ri437\sl249\slmult1\sb4\f0\fs20\b0\expnd0\expndtw0\charscalex100 Figure 2.70.\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 You can select to\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 graph any\expnd-1\expndtw-6  \expnd0\expndtw0 of\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 the outputs of\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 ET, MPH, 60 ft times or the Special Timer results if\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 you have the Team Engineer version.\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\sl240\slmult1\f0\fs20\b0\i0\par
