l240\slmult1\sb119\f1\fs28\b0\expnd-1\expndtw-4\charscalex100 Feet\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li360\ri941\sl249\slmult1\sb249\f0\fs20\b0\expnd0\expndtw0\charscalex100 Is the distance of the race.\expnd13\expndtw63  \expnd0\expndtw0 The \'93Imprvmnts\'94 (amount of improvement in performance between successive runs) in the History is only shown if the runs were for the same distance.\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\sl240\slmult1\f0\fs20\b0\i0\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\sl240\slmult1\sb17\f0\fs20\b0\i0\par\pard\plain\s8\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li360\sl240\slmult1\sb1\f1\fs28\b0\expnd0\expndtw-2\charscalex100 Dnsy\expnd-3\expndtw-13  \expnd-1\expndtw-5 Alt\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li360\ri941\sl249\slmult1\sb248\f0\fs20\b0\expnd0\expndtw0\charscalex100 Density\expnd-1\expndtw-6  \expnd0\expndtw0 Altitude in feet above sea level of\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 the current track weather conditions. Many\expnd-1\expndtw-6  \expnd0\expndtw0 racers like this number for comparisons. It basically means for a standard 29.92" barometer, 60 deg, 0% humidity day what altitude would give the same \f8\b1\i1 barometric\i1  pressure \f0\b0\i0 as the current track conditions.\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\sl240\slmult1\f0\fs20\b0\i0\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\sl240\slmult1\sb18\f0\fs20\b0\i0\par\pard\plain\s8\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li360\sl240\slmult1\f1\fs28\b0\expnd0\expndtw0\charscalex100 Dry\expnd-4\expndtw-19  \expnd0\expndtw0 Dnsy\expnd-4\expndtw-18  \expnd-1\expndtw-5 Alt\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li360\fi-1\ri941\sl249\slmult1\sb249\f0\fs20\b0\expnd0\expndtw0\charscalex100 Dry Density Altitude in feet above sea level of the current track weather conditions, sometimes called Corrected Density Altitude (corrected for humidity). It basically\expnd-1\expndtw-4  \expnd0\expndtw0 means for a standard 29.92" barometer, 60 deg, 0% humidity\expnd-1\expndtw-4  \expnd0\expndtw0 day\expnd-1\expndtw-4  \expnd0\expndtw0 what altitude would give the same \f8\b1\i1 oxygen content \f0\b0\i0 as the current track conditions.\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 This is a better measure than Density\expnd-1\expndtw-3  \expnd0\expndtw0 Altitude for your car\'92s true HP potential.\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\sl240\slmult1\f0\fs20\b0\i0\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\sl240\slmult1\sb19\f0\fs20\b0\i0\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li360\ri9820\sl242\slmult1\f1\fs28\b0\expnd0\expndtw0\charscalex100 60 ft \expnd-1\expndtw-4 Imprvmnt \expnd-1\expndtw-6 ET\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li360\ri9594\sl242\slmult1\sb4\f1\fs28\b0\expnd-1\expndtw-4\charscalex100 Imprvmnt MPH\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li360\sl240\slmult1\sb2\f1\fs28\b0\expnd0\expndtw-2\charscalex100 Imprvmnt\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li360\ri1277\sl249\slmult1\sb249\f0\fs20\b0\expnd0\expndtw0\charscalex100 Are the test results for the particular run.\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 The Imprvmnts are the improvement of a particular run over the previous run. Imprvmnt is left blank if the previous run was not for the same Feet distance as that particular run in the History log.\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\sl240\slmult1\sb11\f0\fs20\b0\i0\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li360\ri1277\sl249\slmult1\f0\fs20\b0\expnd0\expndtw0\charscalex100 If\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 the Feet distances are 5280 ( 1 mile) or 7040 ft (the distance of\expnd-1\expndtw-3  \expnd0\expndtw0 El Mirage), the 60 foot time is actually\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 the 660 foot (1/8 mile) time . If the Feet distance is are 26400 (the distance of Bonneville), the 60 foot time is actually the 2 mile time .\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\sl240\slmult1\f0\fs20\b0\i0\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\sl240\