\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li806\ri8733\sl249\slmult1\f0\fs20\b0\expnd0\expndtw0\charscalex100 You will notice the Converter Capacity was 385 for the V-6 and shows a 7480 RPM for the current Stall RPM. This makes sense since this is was a loose converter for a higher RPM, lower torque producing engine.\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 Now the converter has now been coupled with a\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 high torque big block. Stall speed would be very high.\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 You could pick an example converter or simply\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 enter your known stall RPM of 4500 and press enter.\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 The program respond\expnd-1\expndtw-6  \expnd0\expndtw0 with\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 calculating a Converter Capacity of\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li806\ri8690\sl249\slmult1\sb19\f0\fs20\b0\expnd0\expndtw0\charscalex100 202.5.\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 For Torque Multiplication, we change\expnd-1\expndtw-7  \expnd0\expndtw0 the\expnd-1\expndtw-7  \expnd0\expndtw0 left\expnd0\expndtw-2  \expnd0\expndtw0 over 1.7 from\expnd0\expndtw1  \expnd0\expndtw0 the\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 V-6\expnd0\expndtw1  \expnd0\expndtw0 to\expnd0\expndtw-2  \expnd0\expndtw0 a\expnd1\expndtw4  \expnd-1\expndtw-4 more\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li806\ri437\sl249\slmult1\sb3\f0\fs20\b0\expnd0\expndtw0\charscalex100 typical 2.0. (Notice how\expnd-1\expndtw-3  \expnd0\expndtw0 this Stall RPM is based on the current Power Curve and Track Weather Conditions, which is why\expnd-1\expndtw-6  \expnd0\expndtw0 we entered Weather Specs before going to the Transmission Specs.)\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\sl240\slmult1\sb11\f0\fs20\b0\i0\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li806\ri357\sl249\slmult1\sb1\f0\fs20\b0\expnd0\expndtw0\charscalex100 Click on the Transmission Type combo box and select Pick Example Transmission.\