ain\s8\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li360\sl240\slmult1\f1\fs28\b0\expnd0\expndtw0\charscalex100 Next\expnd-3\expndtw-15  \expnd-1\expndtw-5 Run\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li360\ri941\sl249\slmult1\sb248\f0\fs20\b0\expnd0\expndtw0\charscalex100 Assume you win your first round with a 9.905 ET.\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 For the next round\'92s Throttle Stop prediction you are tempted to use your latest run to help predict a new throttle stop.\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 However, because the difference between Previous Run #1 and your latest run is less than .3 seconds (9.905-9.760 = .145), \f8\b1\i1 the accuracy would not be good and the program recommends you do not do it\f0\b0\i0 . Actually,\expnd3\expndtw13  \expnd0\expndtw0 the program\expnd3\expndtw13  \expnd0\expndtw0 will\expnd3\expndtw13  \expnd0\expndtw0 not\expnd3\expndtw13  \expnd0\expndtw0 even\expnd3\expndtw16  \expnd0\expndtw0 calculate a\expnd3\expndtw13  \expnd0\expndtw0 Throttle Stop\expnd2\expndtw10  \expnd0\expndtw0 setting\expnd2\expndtw10  \expnd0\expndtw0 for\expnd3\expndtw16  \expnd0\expndtw0 the Predicted\expnd2\expndtw10  \expnd0\expndtw0 run\expnd3\expndtw16  \expnd0\expndtw0 if the ETs for\expnd3\expndtw16  \expnd0\expndtw0 the Previous run\expnd3\expndtw16  \expnd0\expndtw0 are not at least .2 seconds or more.\expnd14\expndtw72  \expnd0\expndtw0 So, from now on, simply\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 enter the new weather conditions for each round into the Predicted Run.\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 Enter your estimate of\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 60 foot time, or let the program estimate it, and set the new\expnd-1\expndtw-3  \expnd0\expndtw0 Throttle Stop setting on your timer for the new weather conditions.\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\sl240\slmult1\f0\fs20\b0\i0\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\sl240\slmult1\f0\fs20\b0\i0\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\sl240\slmult1\sb32\f0\fs20\b0\i0\par\pard\plain\s8\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li360\sl240\slmult1\f1\fs28\b0\expnd0\expndtw-2\charscalex100 Conclusions:\par\pard\plain\s11\ls55\ilvl0\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li902\fi-360\ri975\sl249\slmult1\sb244\tx902\f0\fs20\b0\i0\expnd0\expndtw0\charscalex100 The Drag Racing Analyzer Pro can predict a throttle stop setting to run a certain ET (Index) under changing weather conditions, based on 2 previous runs with different throttle stop settings which produce at least .3 seconds difference in \expnd-1\expndtw-4 ET.\par\pard\plain\s11\ls55\ilvl0\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li902\fi-360\ri1016\sl249\slmult1\tx902\f0\fs20\b0\i0\expnd0\expndtw0\charscalex100 Using .001 Sec Increments (instead of .01 Sec Increments in the Preferences menu) lets the program make 60 foot, ET and Throttle Stop predictions in thousandths of a second.\par\sect\sectd\sbkpage\pgnrestart\pgnstarts169\headery731\footery748
