scussed in Section 2.2.\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 Dynamometer tests which measure engine performance can be done in different ways.\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 How the test is done can over-estimate or under-estimate the engine's torque and HP in the vehicle.\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\sl240\slmult1\sb11\f0\fs20\b0\i0\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li360\ri874\sl249\slmult1\sb1\f0\fs20\b0\expnd0\expndtw0\charscalex100 The Drag Racing Analyzer works best if\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 you enter steady\expnd-1\expndtw-6  \expnd0\expndtw0 state dynamometer results, with the engine equipped exactly\expnd-1\expndtw-6  \expnd0\expndtw0 as it will be in the vehicle.\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 "Equipped" means with the full exhaust and intake system, all accessories running like water pump, fan, etc. "Steady state"\expnd3\expndtw13  \expnd0\expndtw0 means\expnd2\expndtw12  \expnd0\expndtw0 that\expnd3\expndtw15  \expnd0\expndtw0 engine\expnd2\expndtw9  \expnd0\expndtw0 RPM\expnd2\expndtw12  \expnd0\expndtw0 is\expnd2\expndtw12  \expnd0\expndtw0 stable\expnd2\expndtw9  \expnd0\expndtw0 (not\expnd3\expndtw15  \expnd0\expndtw0 changing)\expnd3\expndtw13  \expnd0\expndtw0 when\expnd4\expndtw19  \expnd0\expndtw0 the\expnd2\expndtw9  \expnd0\expndtw0 torque\expnd2\expndtw9  \expnd0\expndtw0 and\expnd3\expndtw13  \expnd0\expndtw0 HP\expnd2\expndtw12  \expnd0\expndtw0 are\expnd2\expndtw9  \expnd0\expndtw0 measured.\expnd16\expndtw80  \expnd0\expndtw0 This\expnd2\expndtw12  \expnd0\expndtw0 is\expnd2\expndtw12  \expnd0\expndtw0 sometimes called a \'93step text\'94.\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\sl240\slmult1\sb13\f0\fs20\b0\i0\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li360\ri941\sl249\slmult1\f0\fs20\b0\expnd0\expndtw0\charscalex100 Accelerating dynamometer tests, where the engine speed is constantly increasing (i.e. 300 RPM/sec), can under-estimate an engine's steady state performance.\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 You may think an accelerating test best represents an engine accelerating in a vehicle. However, the Drag Racing Analyzer calculates the power loss due to\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 accelerating the engine, which changes in each gear.\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 See "Inertia" discussion in this Appendix.\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\sl240\slmult1\f0\fs20\b0\i0\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\sl240\slmult1\sb19\f0\fs20\b0\i0\par\pard\plain\s8\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li360\sl240\slmult1\f1\fs28\b0\expnd0\expndtw-2\charscalex100 Rotating\expnd-1\expndtw-7  \expnd0\expndtw-2 Inertia\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li360\ri941\sl249\slmult1\sb249\f0\fs20\b0\expnd0\expndtw0\charscalex100 The difference between\expnd4\expndtw18  \expnd0\expndtw0 stationary and rotating mass is important\expnd3\expndtw14  \expnd0\expndtw0 for\expnd4\expndtw18  \expnd0\expndtw0 a\expnd3\expndtw14  \expnd0\expndtw0 racer\expnd4\expndtw18  \expnd0\expndtw0 to understand.\expnd16\expndtw78  \expnd0\expndtw0 Every racer\expnd4\expndtw18  \expnd0\expndtw0 knows that\expnd3\expndtw14  \expnd0\expndtw0 the less a car weighs, the faster it can accelerate.\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 However, not every\expnd0\expndtw-2  \expnd0\expndtw0 racer knows that removing 30 lbs from the vehicle's rotating components (wheels, tires, engine flywheel) will show\expnd0\expndtw-2  \expnd0\expndtw0 a larger improvement in accelerating performance than removing 30 lbs from the frame or body.\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\sl240\slmult1\sb13\f0\fs20\b0\i0\par
