\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li360\ri7715\sl249\slmult1\f0\fs20\b0\expnd0\expndtw0\charscalex100 This is because not only do you have to accelerate the tires down the quarter mile, you have\expnd-1\expndtw-3  \expnd0\expndtw0 to\expnd-1\expndtw-5  \expnd0\expndtw0 get the\expnd-1\expndtw-3  \expnd0\expndtw0 tires\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 to\expnd-1\expndtw-5  \expnd0\expndtw0 spin faster also. The spare tire in the trunk is easier to accelerate than the same tire mounted on the axle.\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 The tire on the axle has both\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 mass \f8\b1\i1 and \f0\b0\i0 rotational inertia.\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\sl240\slmult1\sb15\f0\fs20\b0\i0\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li360\ri7715\sl249\slmult1\sb1\f0\fs20\b0\expnd0\expndtw0\charscalex100 Rotational inertia is a part's resistance to changing its rotational speed.\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 Jack up the axle and try\expnd-1\expndtw-5  \expnd0\expndtw0 to spin the wheel.\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 Neglecting friction, a heavier wheel requires more force to spin than a light wheel.\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 In addition, if the mass is concentrated in the tire and less in the wheel, it will require even more force to spin.\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 That is because rotational inertia depends on mass and the distance the mass is from the center of rotation.\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 See Figure A1.1.\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\sl240\slmult1\sb19\f0\fs20\b0\i0\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li359\ri941\sl249\slmult1\f0\fs20\b0\expnd0\expndtw0\charscalex100 For this reason, rotating components with small diameters, which concentrate the mass close to the center of rotation, have much less inertia.\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 These components consist of the driveshaft, axle shafts, etc.\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 Reducing the weight of these components insignificantly reduces your rotating inertia\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 Rotating components with larger diameters (flywheel or torque converter, wheels/tires, somewhat in the crankshaft, damper and transmission components) contain most of the vehicle's rotating inertia. These are the components to concentrate on when trying to reduce rotating inertia.\expnd8\expndtw40  \f8\b1\i1\expnd0\expndtw0 For example, removing 1 pound from the\i1  engine\'92s flywheel will have 100 up to 1000 times or more effect on the vehicle\'92s rotational inertia than removing 1 pound from an axle shaft.\par\sect\sectd\sbkpage\headery731\footery748\margtsxn1120\margbsxn940\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\sl240\slmult1\sb37\f8\fs28\b1\i1\par\pard\plain\s8\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li806\sl240\slmult1\f1\fs28\b0\expnd0\expndtw-2\charscalex100 Example\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li806\sl240\slmult1\sb249\f0\fs20\b0\expnd0\expndtw0\charscalex100 Try\expnd-2\expndtw-8  \expnd0\expndtw0 some\expnd0\expndtw-2  \expnd0\expndtw0 examples with\expnd1\expndtw6  \expnd0\expndtw0 the\expnd0\expndtw-2  \expnd0\expndtw0 Drag\expnd0\expndtw1  \expnd0\expndtw0 Racing\expnd0\expndtw1  \expnd0\expndtw0 Analyzer\expnd1\expndtw6  \expnd0\expndtw0 with\expnd1\expndtw5  \expnd0\expndtw0 the\expnd0\expndtw-2  \expnd0\expndtw0 GT5.0L.\expnd11\expndtw56  \expnd0\expndtw0 The\expnd0\expndtw-2  \expnd0\expndtw0 GT5.0L's Baseline\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 performance\expnd0\expndtw-2  \expnd0\expndtw0 is a\expnd1\expndtw3  \expnd0\expndtw0 14.593\expnd0\expndtw1  \expnd-1\expndtw-5 ET.\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\sl240\slmult1\sb20\f0\fs20\b0\i0\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li806\ri437\sl249\slmult1\f0\fs20\b0\expnd0\expndtw0\charscalex100 Now, remove 40 lbs from the front wheels by\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 setting Front Wheels/Tires WT = 10 instead of 50.\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 This modification simulates moving\expnd2\expndtw9  \expnd0\expndtw0 40\expnd2\expndtw9  \expnd0\expndtw0 lbs\expnd2\expndtw8  \expnd0\expndtw0 from\expnd2\expndtw11  \expnd0\expndtw0 the front\expnd2\expndtw11  \expnd0\expndtw0 wheels\expnd2\expndtw8  \expnd0\expndtw0 and\expnd2\expndtw9  \expnd0\expndtw0 placing\expnd2\expndtw9  \expnd0\expndtw0 it\expnd2\expndtw11  \expnd0\expndtw0 somewhere on\expnd3\expndtw15  \expnd0\expndtw0 the body,\expnd3\expndtw13  \expnd0\expndtw0 since we did\expnd2\expndtw9  \expnd0\expndtw0 not\expnd2\expndtw11  \expnd0\expndtw0 also reduce Vehicle Weight\expnd2\expndtw11  \expnd0\expndtw0 40 lbs.\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 (If you have the Preference \'93Warn on Tire Weight Change\'94 selected, the program will ask you if you want to change the vehicle weight\expnd2\expndtw10  \expnd0\expndtw0 by\expnd0\expndtw-2  \expnd0\expndtw0 80\expnd2\expndtw8  \expnd0\expndtw0 lbs when\expnd3\expndtw13  \expnd0\expndtw0 you\expnd2\expndtw8  \expnd0\expndtw0 leave the Wheels/Tires menu.\expnd14\expndtw71  \expnd0\expndtw0 Answer\expnd3\expndtw13  \expnd0\expndtw0 No for\expnd3\expndtw13  \expnd0\expndtw0 now.)\expnd13\expndtw67  \expnd0\expndtw0 Calculate performance an\expnd3\expndtw13  \expnd0\expndtw0 we get\expnd2\expndtw10  \expnd0\expndtw0 an ET of 14.512.\expnd13\expndtw63  \expnd0\expndtw0 Nearly\expnd-1\expndtw-5  \expnd0\expndtw0 a one tenth improvement just by\expnd-1\expndtw-5  \expnd0\expndtw0 moving weight around on the vehicle (not moving it to change traction).\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\sl240\slmult1\sb14\f0\fs20\b0\i0\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li806\ri515\sl249\slmult1\f0\fs20\b0\expnd0\expndtw0\charscalex100 Now\expnd-1\expndtw-3  \expnd0\expndtw0 reduce the Vehicle Weight 80 lbs to\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 3120.\expnd12\expndtw62  \expnd0\expndtw0 This simulates removing 40 lbs from each\expnd2\expndtw9  \expnd0\expndtw0 front wheel & tire\expnd0\expndtw-1  \f8\b1\i1